00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.040
Look how I'm checking that I'm recording before I'm even starting.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.060
I dunno... I get why people enjoy it...

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:24.500
and I = I still...  you can still see me in there
but..... it's so bad *laughs*

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.100
(voiceover) This poster, it shows how gay you are! Look!

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.000
Exposing myself here.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
I don't know - I don't .. really don't like that...

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
I feel like that was...

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.000
I still make kinda stupid jokes that I shouldn't have made, ...

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.580
but I
feel like back then I didn't understand

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:44.460
I was so immature, and I just thought
things were funny just because they were offensive.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.060
So I would say a lot of stupid
shit. I'm not proud of it - I really not.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.400
But I'm also glad that I've grown pass it.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.280
(Voiceover)
"But Dad, he wants to kill..."
"I'm not your Dad"

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.840
Like... this is 23 parts later and I'm still making the same joke about the boy.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.420
It's just the same stuff, over and over.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.620
Also, these videos, I literally just recorded myself, like, 15 minutes.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.100
I probably record now for even five times

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.920
more than that just so I can get
entertaining material and just show the best stuff

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:20.440
Moving on to "Amnesia" -  the show that everyone associates ... the good old Pewdiepie with.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.170
I love this intro.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.880
I get nostalgic just seeing this intro as well

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.640
This is before - eh - "Binding of
Isaac" was popular as well, so no one knew where I stole that graphic art from (chuckles)

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:45.720
(voiceover) "How's it going bros, my name is Peewdiepie"

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.240
I look like such a little shit. (giggles)

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:53.680
(voiceover) "Behind this... I mean I put that in the pi... I put it... Oh god dammed.  I don't remember. I'm a fukin' wrong person ...

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.580
(voiceover) "Alright! Is this really my house???"

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.840
It's funny, cuz I get a lot of comments of people saying

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.080
"Back in the day, he was
so much more natural and didn't force that humor"

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.740
But literally, I was trying so fukin' hard
to make jokes while playing this game.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:15.660
Like, there's literally a part that I accidentally kept in, 
I - I get frustrated because I didn't

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.800
think the video as entertaining, so i say
"God dammit I'm not funny enough!"

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.440
(voiceover) "Yeh, yeh... yeh... yeh. Fuk, I don't feel like I'm funny today..."

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:28.160
We also have this. This is a video I
uploaded by mistake

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.000
It's got 300,000 views.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.680
Back in the day, I
literally did everything last minute...

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.580
like I would make the video, finish the video, upload the video

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.980
and it was such a stressful process to do that.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.040
But here, I wasn't home when I
published this video

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:47.160
Because me and my... I remember me and Marzia went to the cinema and I accidentally uploaded my

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.960
facecam, instead of the actual video, and published it.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:56.600
So it's literally... 11 minutes of me just doing facecam.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.500
I wonder what would happen if I
did that today (chuckles)

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.500
LOOK AT ME! LOOK AT THAT MUSTACHE!!!

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.220
*laughs*

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.580
Ohhh..

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:07.640
I guess so... *laughs*

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.540
*laughs*

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.540
I guess some habits never change!

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:16.060
Goddamn... I love how this is still up...

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.740
Now, "Amnesia", was my baby.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:22.720
"Amnesia" was the - the series that really elevated my channel...

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.640
Here's one episode, from the play-through...

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.060
(voiceover) "That's good."

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.820
"I wanted to go back"

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.920
... of me trying to solve a puzzle

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.900
(voiceover) "I could jam you all day"

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.740
"That's what she said"

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.420
"That's what she said" joke. That's
hilarious (-_-)

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.420
I'm literally stuck on this one puzzle...

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.460
for the entire... episode.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:52.260
Here is me using
"r*tarded" in the title, again.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.960
I was very childish back then. I really should go
through and, like, censor lot of these videos.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.900
(comment) "This was kind of frustrating to
watch. He kept going back and forth in...

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:02.930
... the sewer area instead of going back"

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.180
Uhh, yeah, I know. That's literally it... *chuckles*

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:08.470
My play-throughs were actually horrible. *laughs*

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.740
Man, I was so cute back then. I get it now.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.120
I get it. I did look cuter back then

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.540
And to be fair, I was more scared back then.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:20.980
First time I ever experienced horror games, it's obviously the worst time, you know.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.900
I still get scared, and that's why mainly I don't play horror games anymore, ...

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.500
because, people expect like an epic reaction of me every time, ...

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.780
and unless there's actual jumpscares in the game, I don't really get that scared

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.920
And I still get terrified while playing video games

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:41.820
"Sophie's curse was the last video I uploaded, it did amazing and everyone loved it

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:47.740
And so did I. It still is very fun for me to get
scared of games, just not every single day

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:55.540
Also back... it was also interesting because back then it was so hard to find games to play

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:58.540
You can tell how Youtube has shaped
gaming industry.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:03.760
This is a game called The Lost Souls. It was one of maybe--I could probably count the amount of

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:09.659
horror games before Slenderman on my fingers. Like, there were so few games

00:07:09.659 --> 00:07:13.629
to play that made it for YouTube videos and
this was--this was one that was really good.

00:07:13.629 --> 00:07:17.149
Now there's probably hundreds or
thousands of games like this

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:21.960
Developers have benefited from my
channel but I think I benefited as well

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:26.420
you know, it's a mutual thing...I used to like all of my videos. *laughter*

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:30.320
and good old Fridays
with PewDiePie recorded on a web cam

00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:36.710
not that the quality matters. I've been criticized a lot
for having bad quality but I always thought people don't

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:41.870
care about the quality, they just want good and
entertaining videos. That always comes first.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:48.660
But to be fair this is 13 minutes of me, uncut, just answering questions. Adjusting my webcam.

00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:54.110
I was probably better at being more engaging
with audience, but to be fair my audience

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:59.120
was a lot smaller back then. I feel like
it's been a struggle for me to adjust to

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:03.210
from being so small to so big and still have
a close relationship with the audience

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.620
because that's why I love about YouTube, that's why I always read the comments and

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.330
always interact with you bros, is because that's

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:13.039
something I love doing. If you bros didn't
exist I wouldn't be making videos. Honestly, I

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:17.229
really, really feel like I've gotten that
connection back. We're doing these fine

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:22.009
creation videos together, where I react to you bros' creations and I love that

00:08:22.009 --> 00:08:28.110
and listening to voicemails, reviewing
fanart...all that kind of stuff is so cool

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:32.930
I love that interaction between us. I feel like
for the first time in a long time that

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:36.630
connection is back and that's really
really important to me and instead of, like,

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:42.240
milking one game into one video I do
three games in one video because I

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.790
want it to be the best video it can be, I want it to
be as entertaining as possible

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:51.440
When, really, I could probably just keep these
three separate videos and

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.779
get that money. But honestly, believe it
or not, I care more about that the video

00:08:55.779 --> 00:09:00.720
is entertaining. That always, always comes
first and these type of videos

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:06.269
like Keep Talking and No One Explodes--they got so much editing, so much work into them just to make it

00:09:06.269 --> 00:09:09.040
as funny as possible, as entertaining as
possible

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:14.800
hours upon hours of work to get that done. I
think people forget that. And these videos

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:19.279
are hilarious, thanks to it. I'm sure if
they were uncut a lot of people would

00:09:19.279 --> 00:09:23.029
love it the same way and enjoy it the same
way but not as many people would be able

00:09:23.029 --> 00:09:27.529
to watch that long of a video. That's just the case. To me, the improvement is clear.

00:09:27.529 --> 00:09:32.200
To me, I've grown so much as an entertainer,

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:38.640
as a comedian, but also as a person. I
feel like back then I was very childish and

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.690
very confused. I didn't know what I was doing but
I know I enjoyed it and it really is

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:48.020
thanks to you bros. I always read the comments, I
always listen to feedback and criticism

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:51.440
and I feel like that's an important part

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.150
criticism has really helped me grow

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:59.040
and I'm very happy about that. And more
than anything I am very proud of who I

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.190
am today and I am also excited to keep
improving for the future

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:08.070
Old, new--I feel like it doesn't matter.
I'm going to keep making videos that I

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:13.660
love to make and that hopefully you bros
love to watch and--really, thank you bros, so

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:18.560
much for watching me and supporting me
throughout the years, even though maybe

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:19.600
things are different,

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.560
even though maybe some changes you don't
love. And if you still support me

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:27.970
throughout that, I really, really
appreciate it. I had to make a decision

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:33.490
throughout the years where I said, I want
to make the videos I wanna make. Not only

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:36.790
the ones my fans want to watch because
then I'm not going to be true to myself

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:42.380
and what I do and eventually I'm just
gonna hate myself and what I do.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:46.460
But, yeah. That's it. Old versus new.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:50.240
Either way, thank you. And
if there's one thing that will never

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:57.360
change, it's the brofist. Thank you bros for
supporting me throughout the years.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:59.530
Do you actually brofist on the outro?

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:02.680
Do you wanna do that just for good old times sake?

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.460
Alright, here we go. You ready?

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:08.650
Brofist.

